    "intro_html":  "Zha jiang mian is the Beijing noodle bowl that built the whole category: a dark, salty, fried sauce spooned over noodles with raw cucumber and carrot piled on top for crunch. The traditional version leans on pork belly and fermented bean paste. Ours uses ground turkey with hoisin carrying the sweet-savory bean note, and it comes to \u003cstrong\u003e567 calories and 25 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$3.36\u003c/strong\u003e a bowl (at everyday cost).",
